mixin () {
  public query func getApiDoc() : async Text {
    "# StioAIhacking starter backend API\n\nThis minimal scaffold stores authorization roles only. No application records, content operations, or OQL entities are registered.\n\n## Identity and access\n\nIC calls carry a caller principal. The frontend pins an Internet Identity derivation origin, published at `/.well-known/ii-derivation-origin` when available. An agent already holding the user's Internet Identity authorization must derive the per-app principal against that origin (for example `icp identity link web <name> --app <host>`). Such a delegation acts with the user's full authority in this app until it expires. A different derivation origin produces a different principal.\n\nFor direct API access a signed-in caller calls `_initialize_access_control()` once before role-guarded calls, including guarded queries. The first signed-in initializer becomes `#admin`; subsequent principals become `#user`. Signing in through the app registers its principal, but someone who has never used that frontend remains unregistered, even if they own the app. Anonymous callers are `#guest`; their initialization is a no-op. An unregistered signed-in caller of role queries or assignment traps with `User is not registered`. Anonymous role queries return `#guest` or `false`, whereas anonymous assignment traps with `Unauthorized: Only admins can assign user roles`. The sign-in protocol also initializes access, but this scaffold does not capture verified attributes.\n\n## Public application methods\n\n- `getApiDoc() : text` — query; returns this static Markdown to anyone, including anonymous callers.\n- `_initialize_access_control() : ()` — update; registers the signed-in caller. Repeating it preserves an existing role. No result payload; anonymous calls do nothing.\n- `getCallerUserRole() : { #admin; #user; #guest }` — query; returns caller's role. Unregistered signed-in callers trap.\n- `isCallerAdmin() : bool` — query; tests caller's admin role. Unregistered signed-in callers trap.\n- `assignCallerUserRole(user : principal, role : { #admin; #user; #guest }) : ()` — update; registered admins can overwrite any principal's role. Other registered or anonymous callers trap with `Unauthorized: Only admins can assign user roles`; unregistered signed-in callers trap with `User is not registered`. Repeating the same assignment stores the same value, but changing a role changes authority; confirm state before retrying an uncertain reassignment.\n- `schema() : text` — query; returns a JSON schema as UTF-8 text without requiring registration. There are currently zero entities to discover.\n- `execute(qJson : text) : { rows : vec (vec { name : text; value : variant }); hasMore : bool }` — query; accepts an OQL request encoded as JSON text, not a Candid query record. Results are a Candid record of cells; scalar value tags are `null_`, `bool`, `nat`, `int`, `float`, `text`. `hasMore` signals more rows. Registration is not required. With no entities registered, a valid query naming an entity traps with `OQL: unknown entity '<name>'`; malformed queries trap with `OQL: invalid query — <details>`. A denied entity, if one is introduced later, traps rather than returning an empty set.\n\nThe frontend also uses an Internet Identity sign-in handshake; use the supported Internet Identity flow for it, not ad-hoc application calls.\n\n## Encoding, lifecycle, and retries\n\nPrincipals are IC identities, not site usernames. Roles and OQL cell values are Candid variants. `schema` and `getApiDoc` return UTF-8 text; `schema` is JSON and `execute` takes JSON text but returns Candid, not JSON. There are no timestamps, blobs, application IDs, durations, counters, uploads, jobs, or application lifecycle transitions in this scaffold. There is no background completion to poll; queries are safe to repeat and cannot create records. Check `schema()` before forming an OQL request; no start entity is currently valid.\n\nAuthorization state persists across upgrades. Initialization is idempotent for an already registered caller. Role assignment overwrites its target, including a previously assigned role; confirm the intended state before repeating an update whose outcome is unknown. No method deletes application content. Handle authorization and OQL parsing traps as canister rejects, not as empty query results."
  };
};
